 ### Occupancy Pruning and Bounding Box Shrinkage
-Occupancy Pruning and Bounding Box Shrinkage is a training and inference acceleration technique that pre-calculates an occupancy grid to prune non-occupied points along rays and shrinks the scene bounding box for more accurate modeling [S3]. The occupancy grid is pre-calculated at training steps 2,000 and 4,000. The bounding box is shrunk based on the grid at step 2,000. The grid is kept for scene composition, recorded per object, and used with warped rays to query occupancy [S3]. L1 regularization is applied to the factored matrices for density to encourage sparsity in tensor rank decomposition parameters [S3].
